// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/course/goldenfloat.t27 -- the t27 course on GoldenFloat: a family of floats split by phi
; Source of truth for apps/website/scripts/course-from-spec.mjs (gHashTag/trinity), which reads
; it the way it reads specs/course/ai-numbers.t27: the constant schema, every test block below,
; every widget in specs/widgets/gallery.t27, every lesson spec compiled clean, the Russian bundle
; named by specs/course/goldenfloat-ru.t27. It writes this course into src/lib/course.generated.ts
; (the page at #/goldenfloat) and a byte-identical copy of this file at public/learn/goldenfloat.t27.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN). The Russian words live in the bundle.

; WHAT THE COURSE IS: course 3 of specs/course/courses.t27, 9 modules of 3 lessons each, on the
; GoldenFloat family of arXiv:2606.05017. Modules 1 and 2 (lessons 1 to 6) give the rule and the
; numbers behind it. Module 3 reads the family as one table instead of one lesson per width.
; Module 4 rounds: the GF-T16 operators that round to nearest even. Modules 5 to 7 are GF16 at
; work, the family beside the IEEE widths, and what the GF-T16 operators cost in silicon, from
; real synthesis runs. Module 8 moves the exponent to trits; module 9 rereads the widest rung,
; counts the decode steps and states what the course claims.

; WHAT THE COURSE DOES NOT DO: outside the cost module it says no number of its own. Every other
; lesson quotes only the constants and test values of the spec it opens, and arithmetic of them.
; The cost module (lessons 19 to 21) quotes one named synthesis run per lesson: part
; xc7a200tfbg676-1, yosys 0.67+post, nextpnr-xilinx 0.9.2-107, seed 1, a register-shell bench
; whose empty-shell cost is stated with every marginal number. No lesson extrapolates a cost to
; a width or an operator that was not run. Where a test writes its value in rather than
; computing it, the lesson says so.

; WHAT THE BROWSER RUNS: the browser compiler evaluates the constant asserts of a spec, not its
; function tests. Where a lesson quotes a function (max_value of gf8.t27, phi_split of
; phi_ratio.t27), it says what the spec states or does the arithmetic of the constants in the open.
; Where a comment in a spec disagrees with its own code or with the family table, the lesson says so.
; The synthesis numbers of the cost module come from yosys and nextpnr runs on the bench, not
; from anything the browser ran.

; WHY 27: 3 cubed lessons, 9 modules of 3, the size of a TRI-27 word. Changing the shape changes the tests.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

